Cell["Abstract", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 
   3.97680718244866*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"12465cb7-43fc-4e82-aea7-\
b1ba60dee697"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this notebook, we extend and formalize the \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] Calculus, a computational frontend for unambiguous, \
symbolic tensor calculations in the Wolfram Language. \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] features concise, but unambiguous input like ",
 StyleBox["T[\[ScriptCapitalU][\[Mu]],\[ScriptCapitalD][\[Nu]]]", "Input"],
 " (\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]T, up \[Mu], down \[Nu]\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) \
and typeset output like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["T", "\[Mu]"], "\[Nu]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8fe4d1dd-6064-4b11-b3f5-77e35deaf48f"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 3.976807218345378*^9}, {
   3.976807258054213*^9, 3.976807359325186*^9}, {3.97680761771111*^9, 
   3.976807629196557*^9}, {3.9768330835806427`*^9, 3.97683321568886*^9}, {
   3.976833313200728*^9, 3.976833313201301*^9}, {3.9768333675841*^9, 
   3.976833464643084*^9}, {3.976833515416271*^9, 3.9768335351197453`*^9}, {
   3.976835701531886*^9, 3.976835800218018*^9}, {3.976922884070139*^9, 
   3.976922897482692*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3984ae6a-6a5f-4fe4-860a-\
d21175f4720b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We take the view that Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s existing ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Symbolic Tensors",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/tutorial/SymbolicTensors.\
html"], None},
  ButtonNote->
   "https://reference.wolfram.com/language/tutorial/SymbolicTensors.html"],
  FontSlant->"Italic",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " plus existing repository functions like ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["MetricTensor",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://resources.wolframcloud.com/FunctionRepository/resources/\
MetricTensor/?i=MetricTensor&searchapi=https%3A%2F%2Fresources.wolframcloud.\
com%2FFunctionRepository%2Fsearch"], None},
  ButtonNote->
   "https://resources.wolframcloud.com/FunctionRepository/resources/\
MetricTensor/?i=MetricTensor&searchapi=https%3A%2F%2Fresources.wolframcloud.\
com%2FFunctionRepository%2Fsearch"],
  FontSlant->"Italic",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " and ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["RiemannTensor",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://resources.wolframcloud.com/FunctionRepository/resources/\
RiemannTensor/?i=RiemannTensor&searchapi=https%3A%2F%2Fresources.wolframcloud.\
com%2FFunctionRepository%2Fsearch"], None},
  ButtonNote->
   "https://resources.wolframcloud.com/FunctionRepository/resources/\
RiemannTensor/?i=RiemannTensor&searchapi=https%3A%2F%2Fresources.wolframcloud.\
com%2FFunctionRepository%2Fsearch"],
  FontSlant->"Italic",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " furnish powerful, ",
 StyleBox["backend",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " tools for differential geometry and relativity. \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] on the other hand, focuses on structural logic of tensor \
algebra, thus a ",
 StyleBox["frontend",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " with syntactic and semantic capabilities: "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 3.976807218345378*^9}, {
   3.976807258054213*^9, 3.976807359325186*^9}, {3.97680761771111*^9, 
   3.976807629196557*^9}, {3.9768330835806427`*^9, 3.97683321568886*^9}, {
   3.976833313200728*^9, 3.976833313201301*^9}, {3.9768333675841*^9, 
   3.976833464643084*^9}, {3.976833515416271*^9, 3.9768335351197453`*^9}, {
   3.976835701531886*^9, 3.9768358877335*^9}, {3.976922913194968*^9, 
   3.9769229235053797`*^9}, {3.976922963947506*^9, 3.976922987057685*^9}, {
   3.977100360862001*^9, 
   3.9771003631328783`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d2b8f9a2-e4b5-48a9-abe5-\
d7d78a933477"],

Cell["valence checking (type safety)", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 3.976807218345378*^9}, {
   3.976807258054213*^9, 3.976807365703022*^9}, 
   3.9768334775185337`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"cc9e1d10-182e-4e14-94d8-\
6466d8c3df67"],

Cell["automatic index canonicalization and coalescing", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 3.976807218345378*^9}, {
   3.976807258054213*^9, 3.976807370937777*^9}, {3.976833545261194*^9, 
   3.976833548533648*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e9806e23-5d07-4c0f-8358-\
73d8dad8d97e"],

Cell["collision-free coordinate transformations", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 3.976807218345378*^9}, {
   3.976807258054213*^9, 3.976807381680141*^9}, {3.976833483014674*^9, 
   3.976833483998077*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"03f31fab-e499-4b43-bda1-\
7c10d9a9804e"],

Cell["\<\
\[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] should be useful for applications of \
differential geometry beyond relativity. Differential geometry is enjoying \
rapidly growing utility in computer vision and robotics, and has long been \
central to classical and quantum mechanics, to field theory, and to gauge \
theory. We have expressed interest in these applications in many earlier \
notebooks and plan to revisit some of them, buttressing prior work with \
formal rigour via \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9768076446562653`*^9, 3.9768077675503798`*^9}, {
  3.976833556708728*^9, 3.976833673163127*^9}, {3.976835921485915*^9, 
  3.976835929878889*^9}, {3.9769230337703*^9, 
  3.9769230441179037`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3fa6a177-17b1-428b-b3bb-\
59b27b2efe04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That said, this notebook is the first in a series dedicated specifically to \
general relativity by implementing Eric Poisson\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["A Relativist's Toolkit",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://a.co/d/8pT6XUR"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://a.co/d/8pT6XUR"],
  FontSlant->"Italic",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " in \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD]. We will verify his derivations ",
 StyleBox["ab initio",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", assuring not just correctness, but rigour of the derivation. In the next \
installment (in preparation), we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll cover covariant \
derivatives and the connections for general relativity. After that, we\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll cover geodesics, Lie derivatives, Killing vectors, the \
Levi-Cevita tensor, geodesic deviation, Fermi Normal Coordinates, and \
reproduce famous metrics like Schwarzschild and Kerr."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 3.976807218345378*^9}, {
   3.976807258054213*^9, 3.976807372892746*^9}, {3.9768074213746433`*^9, 
   3.9768076068674717`*^9}, {3.976807777446004*^9, 3.976807855855891*^9}, {
   3.976831541286274*^9, 3.9768315519650793`*^9}, {3.976831585041976*^9, 
   3.976831622357461*^9}, {3.976831661271888*^9, 3.976831792670689*^9}, {
   3.976833681362753*^9, 3.976833974657584*^9}, {3.976835981779799*^9, 
   3.9768360007192583`*^9}, {3.976923050230913*^9, 3.976923070941328*^9}, {
   3.977100407913069*^9, 
   3.977100576167754*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0cbf9991-3593-4696-a6be-\
cf276cef1fe6"],

Cell["\<\
All along, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll incrementally develop , a \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] compiler backend: a translation layer to map \
\[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] expressions onto \
Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s existing SymbolicTensor and elements of the \
function repository. Our objective is that users can derive physical laws in \
the high-assurance \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] environment and then \
seamlessly compile them to Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s computational \
infrastructure. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 3.976807218345378*^9}, {
   3.976807258054213*^9, 3.976807372892746*^9}, {3.9768074213746433`*^9, 
   3.9768076068674717`*^9}, {3.976807777446004*^9, 3.976807855855891*^9}, {
   3.976831541286274*^9, 3.9768315519650793`*^9}, {3.976831585041976*^9, 
   3.976831622357461*^9}, {3.976831661271888*^9, 3.976831792670689*^9}, {
   3.976833681362753*^9, 3.976833974657584*^9}, {3.976835981779799*^9, 
   3.9768360603819313`*^9}, {3.976923102553553*^9, 3.976923138266436*^9}, {
   3.977100582079254*^9, 
   3.977100642885683*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fb11a969-3871-4722-a943-\
fd639187fa61"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] is an exercise in formal \
(machine-checked) mathematics with compiler-like architecture. While the \
Wolfram language is not, ",
 StyleBox["prima facie",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", a purely formal system like Rocq, Lean, or TLA+, \
Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s symbolic algebra lets us have many formal checks, \
not to mention numerical agility, throughout any work. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 3.976807218345378*^9}, {
   3.976807258054213*^9, 3.976807372892746*^9}, {3.9768074213746433`*^9, 
   3.9768076068674717`*^9}, {3.976807777446004*^9, 3.976807855855891*^9}, {
   3.976831541286274*^9, 3.9768315519650793`*^9}, {3.976831585041976*^9, 
   3.976831622357461*^9}, {3.976831661271888*^9, 3.976831792670689*^9}, {
   3.976833681362753*^9, 3.976834036825973*^9}, {3.976836069495987*^9, 
   3.9768361274544888`*^9}, {3.976923160374092*^9, 3.976923175103085*^9}, 
   3.977100657181278*^9},ExpressionUUID->"0a2f6dc6-b1b5-48d5-a59b-\
918d790381f7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.976805343965353*^9, {3.976807171258144*^9, 3.976807218345378*^9}, {
